course: dictionary
lesson: 660
title: A word from France
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A baguette is a long, thin loaf of white bread with a crisp crust. Context helps you find its meaning: «Mum bought a fresh baguette from the bakery.» You buy it at a bakery, so it must be a kind of bread.
explain: The word can also mean a sandwich made with this bread. «We ate a ham baguette for lunch.» You eat it for lunch and it has ham in it, so here it means a sandwich. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Words can travel between languages. Baguette comes from French, the language of France, where this bread was first made. When English borrowed the word, it kept its French spelling, so it looks a little different from English words.
fact: A baguette is a long, thin loaf of white bread with a crisp crust.
fact: A baguette can also mean a sandwich made with this bread.
fact: The baguette was first made in France.
fact: English took many food words from French, including menu, café, croissant and baguette.
fact: «Un jambon-beurre» is a baguette with ham and butter, one of the most popular sandwiches in France.
exercise: «Mum bought a fresh baguette from the bakery.» What is a baguette? | A kind of bicycle | A pair of shoes | A type of cheese | *A long, thin loaf of white bread
exercise: «We ate a ham baguette for lunch.» What does ham baguette mean here? | *A sandwich made with a baguette and ham | A ham bone | A loaf with no crust | A French car
exercise: Which country was the baguette first made in? | Germany | Italy | *France | Spain
test: Which of these words came into English from French? | Table | Chair | Dog | *Croissant
test: In French, «one» before a feminine word is «une». Which word means «one» in «une baguette»? | la | un | le | *une
exam: Jayden says a baguette can only be a sandwich. What is the best answer? | It is always a cake | It is a type of bus | *It can be a loaf of bread or a sandwich made with bread | It is a kind of fish
